WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.437
The federal requirement.

2
00:00:01.437 --> 00:00:08.163
The controls are from NIST SP 800-53,
Revision 5, at the Moderate baseline.

3
00:00:08.163 --> 00:00:11.126
Every runbook step has
a requirements table,

4
00:00:11.126 --> 00:00:16.012
and every step leaves an evidence record
that names its controls and KSIs.

5
00:00:16.012 --> 00:00:20.975
The pre-flight check meets C M three,
enhancement two: the settings, kits,

6
00:00:20.975 --> 00:00:24.654
identities and cloud are
checked before any change,

7
00:00:24.654 --> 00:00:28.162
and pre-flight dot json is
the evidence, dry and live.

8
00:00:28.162 --> 00:00:32.953
Its rows P F oh two and P F oh five
show no secret in the settings file and

9
00:00:32.953 --> 00:00:38.751
three certificate identities, for
authenticator management and least privilege.

10
00:00:38.751 --> 00:00:43.332
The smoke test reads the gates' checks
again after the change and answers

11
00:00:43.332 --> 00:00:47.838
go or no-go, for the verification of
controls and continuous monitoring.

12
00:00:47.838 --> 00:00:53.162
One evidence package with a hash per file,
verified, protects the audit information.

13
00:00:53.162 --> 00:00:57.088
And every change is recorded
with its rollback, newest first.

14
00:00:57.088 --> 00:01:00.968
The KSI column is from FedRAMP's
Key Security Indicators,

15
00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:04.435
which are indicators for
cloud service providers;

16
00:01:04.435 --> 00:01:09.700
Chapter 10 uses only KSI IDs this workbook
already maps to the same controls.
